       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. That is five times the usual maximum for an adult, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. A single 4000 mg dose is also about 10 times the usual single dose of 400 to 800 mg. A dose this high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and CNS and metabolic toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg** PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg** PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg** PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 4000 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly and give me the clinical rationale for the order note."
